{"type":"step-attempt","step":"cross-boundary-invariants","sessionId":"4d33fdd6-2283-4f69-b765-81ab04efa320","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/issue-target-resume-from-issue/cross-boundary-invariants-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":false,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/resume-from-issue.ts","title":"slug がリバインド後に verified.slug へ更新されず runResumeCore に古い resolved.slug が渡される","rationale":"needsRebind=true 経路で slug は L143 で resolved.slug に設定される（identity check の checkpointOid₁ 由来）。setupWorkspace は L186 で verified.slug（runAttachVerification の checkpointOid₂ 由来）を使用する。remote branch が 2 回の fetch の間に force-push されて change folder 名が変わった場合、setupWorkspace は新 slug でワークスペースを作成し、runResumeCore は旧 slug でローカル state を探すため、resolveJobStateBySlug が state を見つけられず resume が失敗する。attach.ts は verified.slug のみを使用しており同問題はない。修正: setupWorkspace 完了後に slug = verified.slug を追加する（1 行）。","line":215}],"evidence":{"checked":14,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/issue-target/resume.ts","title":"resolved.checkpointOid が計算されるが resume-from-issue.ts で使用されない","rationale":"resolveResumeBranchFromIssue の戻り値 checkpointOid は呼び出し元で捨てられ、setupWorkspace には verified.checkpointOid（runAttachVerification 由来）が使われる。設計 D3 の意図には適合するが、戻り値インターフェースに不使用フィールドが存在し誤誘導になりうる。正確性への影響はない。","line":88},{"severity":"low","file":"src/cli/__tests__/resume-from-issue.test.ts","title":"TC-001 は resolved.slug と verified.slug の乖離シナリオを pin しない","rationale":"TC-001 の両モックが同じ slug を返すため、Finding の修正（slug = verified.slug）適用後もテストは通過するが、乖離ケースの pin が不足する。Finding の修正後に diverge ケースを pin するテストを追加することが望ましい。","line":262}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-20T10:48:03.984Z","endedAt":"2026-08-20T10:56:01.278Z"}
{"type":"step-attempt","step":"scale-tolerance","sessionId":"bea2f033-901d-4232-b46d-29cb1bcd1c98","outcome":{"verdict":"escalation","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/issue-target-resume-from-issue/scale-tolerance-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":false,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/issue-target/resume.ts","title":"Comment scan always fetches all pages — O(⌈C/100⌉) API calls growing with issue discussion","rationale":"`resolveEscalationJobId` calls `listIssueComments` which paginates all comment pages (per_page=100, follows Link header). GitHub returns comments ascending by default, so the newest escalation marker is always on the last page — no early exit is possible. The local-state short-circuit (D4) runs AFTER the comment scan, so every invocation unconditionally pays the full pagination cost. Comments grow monotonically (discussion, notifications, repeated escalation cycles). Fix: add direction=desc to fetch newest-first and stop after finding the first marker page.","line":54},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/issue-target/resume.ts","title":"Full checkpoint read (events.jsonl + ls-tree) performed for non-confirming branch candidates","rationale":"`readCheckpointFromRef` reads state.json + events.jsonl + full tree listing for each linked-branch candidate. Only state.json is needed for the identity check. events.jsonl grows monotonically with job duration; ls-tree -r enumerates all checkpoint artifacts. For non-confirming candidates these are read and discarded. Bounded by first:50 candidates and typically one linked branch per issue. Fix: lightweight readStateJsonFromRef variant for identity-check phase.","line":152},{"severity":"low","resolution":"decision-needed","file":"src/adapter/github/github-client.ts","title":"linkedBranches(first:50) and closedByPullRequestsReferences(first:50) silently truncate with no cursor","rationale":"Both GraphQL connections cap at 50 with no pageInfo/cursor. An issue with >50 linked branches (long-running epic, many restart cycles) silently omits excess. If the valid resume branch is beyond position 50, the command fails with RESUME_FROM_ISSUE_UNCONFIRMED — misleading when the branch exists but was truncated. Design explicitly documents this cap as accepted.","line":743,"options":[{"label":"Accept first:50 cap (status quo)","consequence":"Operators with >50 linked branches must fall back to job attach --branch manually; acceptable given the documented bound and rarity of the condition"},{"label":"Add GraphQL cursor pagination for both connections","consequence":"Correct at unlimited scale; requires additional GraphQL roundtrips beyond the first 50; added implementation complexity"}]}],"evidence":{"checked":7,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/job-access/load-by-job-id.ts","title":"Pre-existing O(N) fallback scan of specrunner/changes/ — new call path added by this PR","rationale":"loadStateByJobId has a fallback that reads every non-archived state.json to match jobId. In the resume --from-issue primary path (no local state), this scan always runs and returns JOB_NOT_FOUND. Code is pre-existing; this PR adds a new caller. Bounded by concurrent active (non-archived) job count, not historical total.","line":82},{"severity":"low","file":"src/adapter/github/github-client.ts","title":"listIssueLinkedBranches: single GraphQL query regardless of branch count — well-bounded","rationale":"The Development-link enumeration issues exactly one GraphQL POST and returns up to 100 branch names (50 + 50). No pagination; constant cost per invocation.","line":737}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-20T10:48:03.984Z","endedAt":"2026-08-20T10:53:48.279Z"}
